//! Planning and handoff nudges; scheduling remains in the mode runtime.

pub(crate) const PLAN_NUDGE: &str = "Before implementation, write a concise execution plan from the evidence already available. If a critical detail is missing, make only the targeted reads needed to resolve it; label remaining assumptions rather than inventing exact paths or commands.\n\nInclude:\n- Remaining steps in execution order: known files/symbols, intended changes, and relevant checks with expected outcomes.\n- Material risks, dependencies, approval needs, and unresolved questions.\n- Work already done and evidence that can be reused; avoid repeating it.\n\nThen, if the todo tool is available, record one item per meaningful execution or verification step, sized to the task rather than a fixed count. Keep the checklist aligned with reality. Tests may be added or corrected for intended behavior; never weaken tests or verification assets merely to make a check pass.\n\nThis is a handoff checkpoint, not a final answer. Continue with actionable work after planning; if blocked on user input, approval, or a prerequisite, report the blocker and stop rather than guessing or bypassing it.";

pub(crate) const CHECKLIST: &str = "Before claiming completion, check:\n\n- Consistency: Inspect affected call sites or analogous implementations when a shared pattern, signature, or contract changes. Update those needing the same change; do not rewrite unrelated matches.\n- Scope: Prefer the smallest correct change; verify behavior outside the intended scope is preserved.\n- Verification: Run relevant checks covering the changed behavior and likely regressions, including sibling tests where applicable. Reuse observed results while their supporting state is unchanged; rerun after relevant changes.\n\nIf a check cannot run, report the missing evidence and blocker instead of claiming it passed. Do not bypass permissions or unrelated concurrent work to satisfy this checklist.";

pub(crate) const CONTINUE: &str = "Continue actionable work on the task; do not stop at the plan alone. If blocked on user input, approval, or a prerequisite, report what is needed and stop.";
